   "id": "co_lucky_strike",
   "area_id": "co_gladstone_peak",
   "name": "Lucky Strike",
   "grade": "5.7",
   "discipline": "ice",
   "overview": "Gladstone Peak's south face: snow that steepens slowly, then AI3 and easy mixed pitches up the center, then the triangular upper headwall, where rock along its right edge gains the south ridge about 200 ft under the summit. P1-2: steep snow. P3: two rockbands, easy (AI3/3+ 5.5); ledges for roping up run out near the ice top, so tie in on the pitches below. P4 (5.7, crux): icy chimney on the right, with an exposed handcrack on its right wall past the first chockstone; belay on the long, narrow ledge about 40 ft up. P5 (5.5): chimney continues. P6: easier, chossier rock to a south-ridge notch, then a steep scramble of a couple hundred feet. Crampons recommended; the party used twin 100' ropes.",
